I can't draw an interactive map in this chat, so below is a self-contained map file and the data behind it. Save the code as `argentina_lithium.html` and open it in a browser. **The coordinates are approximate**, placed at salar or district centres, except Cauchari-Olaroz and Centenario-Ratones, whose coordinates come from a government portfolio. For publication, replace them with coordinates from the SEGEMAR or provincial mining registries.

## What's on the map

**Producing brine operations**
The seven projects in commercial production are Cauchari-Olaroz, Centenario-Ratones, Fénix, Mariana, Olaroz, Sal de Oro and Tres Quebradas.

- Cauchari-Olaroz is in Jujuy. Its 2026 guidance is roughly 35,000 to 40,000 tonnes of lithium carbonate.
- Fénix is in the Salar del Hombre Muerto, Catamarca. It was the only operating lithium project in Argentina for almost 20 years.
- Olaroz (Jujuy) was the second operation to start, in 2015, per the same report.
- Tres Quebradas is in Fiambalá, Catamarca.

**Under construction or ramping up (not yet producing)**
Hombre Muerto Oeste, Rincón, Sal de los Ángeles, Sal de Vida and Salar del Rincón are under construction. I've plotted them in a different colour for context.

**Past-producing (hard-rock pegmatites)**
These are small, historical operations in the Pampean Pegmatite Province.

- In San Luis, the "Maria del Huerto" dykes were mined for spodumene between 1936 and 1940.
- The Conlara district in San Luis is one of the most heavily mined districts of the province and produced beryl, mica, feldspar and quartz, plus minor tantalum and bismuth minerals.
- In Catamarca, the Ancasti and Vilisman pegmatite groups have old workings. Latin Resources described both as having past lithium mining activity.
- Las Tapias (Córdoba/San Luis) was a large beryl producer, with spodumene resources partly mined in the past. I left it off the map because I couldn't confirm its coordinates.

I did not find a reliable list of individual past-producing pegmatite mines with coordinates. The pegmatite points are district-level markers, not mine locations.

## Map code (Leaflet)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Lithium in Argentina</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" />
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"></script>
  <style>
    html, body, #map { height: 100%; margin: 0; }
    .legend { background: white; padding: 8px 10px; line-height: 1.5; border-radius: 4px; }
    .dot { display:inline-block; width:10px; height:10px; border-radius:50%; margin-right:6px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
const map = L.map('map').setView([-26, -66.5], 6);
L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png',
  { attribution: '© OpenStreetMap contributors' }).addTo(map);

const colors = { producing: '#d62728', construction: '#ff9900', past: '#1f77b4' };

// name, lat, lon, status, province, note  (coordinates approximate)
const sites = [
  ["Cauchari-Olaroz", -23.42, -66.71, "producing", "Jujuy", "Brine; Minera Exar"],
  ["Olaroz", -23.45, -66.75, "producing", "Jujuy", "Brine"],
  ["Centenario-Ratones", -25.09, -66.82, "producing", "Salta", "Brine; Eramet"],
  ["Fénix (Hombre Muerto)", -25.43, -66.95, "producing", "Catamarca", "Brine; since 1990s"],
  ["Sal de Oro", -25.35, -66.95, "producing", "Catamarca", "Brine; POSCO"],
  ["Mariana", -24.55, -68.45, "producing", "Salta", "Brine; Ganfeng"],
  ["Tres Quebradas", -27.00, -68.10, "producing", "Catamarca", "Brine; Zijin/LIEX"],
  ["Sal de Vida", -25.55, -66.90, "construction", "Catamarca", "Brine; Rio Tinto"],
  ["Hombre Muerto Oeste", -25.40, -67.10, "construction", "Catamarca", "Brine; Galan"],
  ["Rincón", -24.15, -67.50, "construction", "Salta", "Brine; Rio Tinto"],
  ["Sal de los Ángeles", -25.00, -66.70, "construction", "Salta", "Brine"],
  ["Ancasti / Vilisman pegmatites", -28.80, -65.40, "past", "Catamarca", "Historic spodumene/lepidolite workings"],
  ["Conlara–Estanzuela pegmatites (incl. Maria del Huerto)", -32.30, -65.90, "past", "San Luis", "Spodumene mined 1936–1940 at Maria del Huerto"]
];

sites.forEach(s => {
  L.circleMarker([s[1], s[2]], {
    radius: 8, color: '#333', weight: 1, fillColor: colors[s[3]], fillOpacity: 0.9
  }).addTo(map).bindPopup(`<b>${s[0]}</b><br>${s[4]}<br>${s[5]}<br><i>Status: ${s[3]}</i>`);
});

const legend = L.control({ position: 'bottomleft' });
legend.onAdd = () => {
  const d = L.DomUtil.create('div', 'legend');
  d.innerHTML =
    `<div><span class="dot" style="background:${colors.producing}"></span>Producing (brine)</div>
     <div><span class="dot" style="background:${colors.construction}"></span>Under construction / ramp-up</div>
     <div><span class="dot" style="background:${colors.past}"></span>Past-producing (pegmatite districts)</div>`;
  return d;
};
legend.addTo(map);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

